# B-LANGSTON-RELIEF (2026-10-19): rotation for the logs the ROOT-run Langston tools write.
# They live in /opt/langston-memory/state (root:root 0755), readable by langston and writable only by root, so
# logrotate runs as root here and needs no `su` (contrast logrotate/langston-recall-usage, whose directory langston
# owns). Same policy as before the move: weekly, 8 kept, compressed. copytruncate keeps each file's inode and its
# root:root 0644 mode. The privacy-check log is included: it was root-written and had no rotation at all.
/opt/langston-memory/state/load-canary.jsonl
/opt/langston-memory/state/size-watch.jsonl
/opt/langston-memory/state/selfmemory-backup.jsonl
/opt/langston-memory/state/privacy-check.jsonl
/opt/langston-memory/state/pattern-promotion.jsonl {
    weekly
    rotate 8
    compress
    missingok
    notifempty
    copytruncate
}
